{"step_index":157,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:32:04Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-16T23:02:04+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-16T23:02:15+05:30\nThe search for \"\"puppeteer\" \"SVG stroke\" \"animation\" record video github\" returned the following summary:\nTo record an SVG stroke animation using Puppeteer, you can leverage several open-source tools on GitHub that automate the process of capturing browser frames and encoding them into video files using FFmpeg.\n\n### Recommended GitHub Projects\nSeveral projects specifically handle the conversion of animated SVGs (including CSS and SMIL animations) into video formats like MP4:\n\n*   **[jcubic/svg-video](https://github.com/jcubic/svg-video):** A robust tool that analyzes your SVG, calculates the animation duration, generates a controlled HTML environment, records the output with Puppeteer, and uses FFmpeg to process it into an MP4 video.\n*   **[freder/svg-animation-to-video](https://github.com/freder/svg-animation-to-video):** A specialized repository focused on rendering animated SVGs to video using Puppeteer and FFmpeg.\n*   **[amirlogic/animated-svg-to-video](https://github.com/amirlogic/animated-svg-to-video):** Another dedicated solution for recording SVG and CSS animations from a webpage into video formats.\n\n### General Approach\nIf you prefer to build a custom solution or understand how these tools work, the general process involves:\n\n1.  **Setup HTML/SVG:** Ensure your SVG is embedded in an HTML page where the animation can trigger automatically (e.g., on page load).\n2.  **Puppeteer Recording:**\n    *   Use the `puppeteer-screen-recorder` library or the native Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) to capture frames from the browser page.\n    *   Initialize the recorder before the animation starts and stop it once the animation completes.\n3.  **FFmpeg Processing:** Since Puppeteer captures raw frames or high-frequency screenshots, you will need **FFmpeg** installed on your system to encode these frames into a final video file (MP4, WebM, etc.).\n\n### Important Considerations\n*   **Timing:** For deterministic results, avoid relying on real-time animations if possible. Some advanced workflows involve \"time virtualization,\" where you pause the animation and manually advance it frame-by-frame to take screenshots, ensuring every frame is captured correctly regardless of performance.\n*   **SVG Dimensions:** Ensure your SVG has either `width`/`height` attributes or a `viewBox` attribute. Missing dimensions are a common cause of failure in automated recording scripts.\n*   **Dependencies:** Most of these tools require system-level dependencies (like `libgtk-3-0`, `libnss3`, etc.) to run Headless Chrome correctly on Linux environments.\n\nFor a step-by-step video guide on the underlying approach of using Puppeteer to convert SMIL or CSS SVG animations into video, you can refer to [this guide on YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SomeVideoID), which covers setting up the rendering script and combining frames into a video."}
{"step_index":158,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:32:04Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-16T23:02:04+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-16T23:02:21+05:30\nThe search for \"\"blender\" \"grease pencil\" auto draw \"whiteboard\" script github\" returned the following summary:\nTo achieve a \"whiteboard\" drawing effect in Blender using Grease Pencil, you generally do not need a complex custom script. The most common and effective method relies on built-in tools.\n\n### Recommended Approach: The Build Modifier\nInstead of using a script, the standard workflow for whiteboard animations involves the **Build Modifier**[1][2][3]:\n\n1.  **Draw your artwork:** Use the Grease Pencil tool to draw your subject[4]. Blender automatically records the order, speed, and timing of your strokes as you draw them[2].\n2.  **Add the Build Modifier:** Select your Grease Pencil object, go to the **Modifiers** tab, and add a **Build** modifier.\n3.  **Configure:** In the modifier settings, you can choose the \"Build\" mode (which draws strokes in sequence) to create the \"auto-draw\" effect[1][2]. You can adjust the frame start, duration, and transition behavior to time the animation to your needs[3].\n\n### GitHub Scripts & Add-ons\nIf you are looking for automation specifically, there are community-made tools that extend this functionality:\n\n*   **GreaseWriter:** This is a well-known GitHub project designed to auto-animate Grease Pencil strokes and emulate hand-drawn text[1][5]. It provides a \"Reanimate\" feature that can help create a polished hand-drawn look[1][6].\n    *   *Search GitHub for:* `doakey3/GreaseWriter`[7]\n*   **Custom Python Scripts:** If you are interested in writing your own automation, users often share snippets on GitHub Gists[8]. Note that if you are using recent versions of Blender (4.0+), you must ensure the script is compatible with the updated **Grease Pencil V3 API**, as older scripts may throw syntax errors[9][10].\n\n### Tips for Whiteboard Animation\n*   **The \"Hand\" Effect:** To make it look like a hand is actually drawing, animate an image of a hand (on a separate plane) using a simple parent constraint to follow the path of your strokes, or use an existing curve to drive the hand's movement[2].\n*   **Tutorials:** Many creators provide step-by-step guides for \"Whiteboard Explainer\" animations in Blender[11][12][13]. Searching for *\"Blender Whiteboard Animation Tutorial\"* on YouTube will provide visual workflows that are often easier to follow than raw code[14][15].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGSnpT9X9MV7KR2jtFIClzujHgseLB_4qZkFDHtj94OI2to3YNAHm_j4j5p7NGCGMhK9XnrD4RXtOgCxsSu4AYTMkyz3XzuEKWEVblbzyr-Lhq9HzL85uQdvqHjz9w=)\n[2] [blenderartists.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFmAYJU9fxXXj4luM6kebgNxmmQlq6eQfAyr2eZDVV5QikA1QuKBtdAnRowc1ROWtNiLi0wP62ELUQdMvvzJ0Rh1febO-jLR1fahtEepXraVofyoFRq7YUUrvwNfxb8jAPsCV7_8ThXH_iUT6-_Bve2tuB9whYsRhhi)\n[3] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE3yiEg_W4Z0iHEuFbWCFcItR6KhOTI8Gwj6jAdI0nv8E6LvrIN0TSCCgmH-k_pvri_U_QRO8oSUeQGdNjuD6tT5M8LpfeSJR-N4AK6cCQn3mGOmXp70fHGCOB2m-lkzwbZ)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGs59t9jxg-5c3nABOK3_4PgdCVB9BNocIr6coq_irloEgNo_yBmN5e9zd-xun3GyGmFoI865acZXwavSF5YiiMOp9Qj_kUYB7L9YzIAKAikwg3ppScM4E8d3AClVoMLQF3YmWmF02WA-Zzd_sjiptBakbR2f7-uk_iMlVC-RX8uQee6dyEpmDsReDiYBs=)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGSnpT9X9MV7KR2jtFIClzujHgseLB_4qZkFDHtj94OI2to3YNAHm_j4j5p7NGCGMhK9XnrD4RXtOgCxsSu4AYTMkyz3XzuEKWEVblbzyr-Lhq9HzL85uQdvqHjz9w=)\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGSnpT9X9MV7KR2jtFIClzujHgseLB_4qZkFDHtj94OI2to3YNAHm_j4j5p7NGCGMhK9XnrD4RXtOgCxsSu4AYTMkyz3XzuEKWEVblbzyr-Lhq9HzL85uQdvqHjz9w=)\n[7] [blender-